| Targeted Attacks on Diffusion Customization | agHddsQhsL.md | 7.5 | Stronger novelty (targeted > untargeted insight); FaceLinkGen's core insight (pixel ≠ identity) is important but the attack methodology is more straightforward |

FaceLinkGen sits between the 5.33 and 6.0 anchors. It has a genuinely important conceptual contribution (the evaluation paradigm critique), comprehensive evaluation with cross-API verification, and the constrained attack is a real insight. The main factor preventing a higher score is the abstract's selective reporting of favorable metrics while omitting the substantially lower 1-to-N linkage numbers. The paper is clearly above the low-scoring anchors (which had fundamental flaws like false novelty claims or missing baselines) and comparable to the medium-scoring anchors that demonstrate evaluation inadequacy in related domains.

