This paper falls below the Chebyshev and Latent Point Collapse anchors (both ~4.25–4.67) because its experiments are more severely flawed (random-chance baseline in 1 of 3 tasks, no meaningful comparison to SAM, unverified mechanism). It is comparable to or slightly below the LCN anchor (3.0) in quality, though it does at least formulate something mathematically clean. The fatal flaw is that the paper's central mechanism claim (finding flatter minima) is never actually verified, and the "consistent improvement" claim is contradicted by the data.

